Subject: [PATCH] wasm: Queue browser resize events

Browser window and VisualViewport resize callbacks enter Wasm directly.
Updating screen geometry there can call application code that uses JSPI
imports, such as synchronizing a file while handling a resize event.
Post the resize to the Qt event loop so the handler can suspend.

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/wasm/qwasmintegration.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/wasm/qwasmintegration.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wasm/qwasmintegration.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wasm/qwasmintegration.cpp
@@ -435,8 +435,12 @@
 
 void QWasmIntegration::resizeAllScreens()
 {
-    for (const auto &elementAndScreen : m_screens)
-        elementAndScreen.wasmScreen->updateQScreenSize();
+    // Browser resize listeners are not JSPI entry points. Publish geometry
+    // through the Qt event loop, where application resize handlers can suspend.
+    QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this] {
+        for (const auto &elementAndScreen : m_screens)
+            elementAndScreen.wasmScreen->updateQScreenSize();
+    }, Qt::QueuedConnection);
 }
 
 void QWasmIntegration::loadLocalFontFamilies(emscripten::val families)
